# ZR (hand-back, first step): status, a PCI rescan for a missing board and the reset of all four cards together. A board that lost its by-id link comes back here. The reset step first removes the job-owned containers a box may have left (a replay, a smoke, a prefix arm), because one of them holds the cards; a platform serving container is never touched. LM and Z run ONLY if ZR passed.
# READ: every board present, the reset clean on all four. A reset renumbers /dev/tenstorrent, so the links are re-measured next (LM, a driver step).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the second chained session of 2026-10-08 (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it). ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags
# and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its default); tp4-serve-10 is the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box:
# the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run. NO profile of this pack carries a digest or an audit (QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS, QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT, the lever audits): test_tp4_session_0808b pins that.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status rescan reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
